WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.380
A behavioral baseline is a maintained reference for expected assets, communication paths, protocols, timing, roles, and operations.

2
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:16.200
OT environments often have repeatable patterns, but a useful baseline must represent more than one quiet afternoon.

3
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:25.280
Observe normal production, startup, shutdown, failover, batch changes, seasonal conditions, and planned maintenance where relevant.

4
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:34.740
Record which devices communicate, which engineering pathways are approved, when remote support occurs, and which commands or sessions belong to each operating mode.

5
00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:45.500
Anomalies may include a new asset, unexpected peer, changed protocol, unusual timing, new engineering session, abnormal write, or activity outside an authorized window.

6
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:49.520
An anomaly is evidence of change, not proof of a cyber event.

7
00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:55.700
Equipment faults, replacement, troubleshooting, and process transitions can create the same signal.

8
00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:59.980
Operator and engineering context reduces false positives.

9
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:07.680
Enrich alerts with work orders, maintenance windows, asset role, process state, and known configuration changes.

10
00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:14.500
Capture the disposition so repeated approved activity can be handled consistently without suppressing unrelated risk.

11
00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:17.660
Known normal is not automatically known good.

12
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:25.840
A learning period may include legacy misconfiguration, unmanaged vendor access, or communication that violates the approved architecture.

13
00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:30.580
Compare observed behavior with policy and design before treating it as trusted.

14
00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.220
Version and review baselines as the environment changes.

15
00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:39.040
Measure whether anomaly logic produces actionable investigation rather than noise.

16
00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:50.500
The strongest approach combines statistical or behavioral deviation with explicit rules, asset criticality, and human context, allowing detection to adapt without losing operational meaning.
